WEBVTT

00:17:29.419 --> 00:17:31.421
Jeanette Winterson: “Don’t fuck it up.”

00:17:31.463 --> 00:17:33.256
OK. I want to talk about love.

00:17:33.298 --> 00:17:36.343
So in your memoir,
which everybody should read,

00:17:36.384 --> 00:17:38.845
it is called “Why Be Happy
When You Can Be Normal?”

00:17:38.887 --> 00:17:40.764
The very end of that book is about --

00:17:40.806 --> 00:17:43.683
it’s a good title -- t’s about love.

00:17:43.683 --> 00:17:46.937
And you write, "Love, the difficult word.

00:17:46.937 --> 00:17:49.272
Where everything starts,
where we always return.

00:17:49.272 --> 00:17:51.900
Love. Love's lack.
The possibility of love."

00:17:51.900 --> 00:17:54.486
Now I don't want
to bastardize Ada Lovelace.

00:17:54.486 --> 00:17:55.946
She was all about originating.

00:17:55.946 --> 00:17:57.531
But what about love?

00:17:57.531 --> 00:18:00.200
What about alternative
intelligence and love?